  <div id="sutta">
  
            <h4 id="StNp5.12" class="h1">5:12  Bhadrāvudha’s Question</h4>
            <div class="verse">
              <p>I entreat the one who has</p>
              <p>abandoned home—cutting through craving, unperturbed;</p>
              <p>abandoned delight—crossed over the flood, released;</p>
              <p>abandoned theory—very intelligent:</p>
              <p>Having heard the Nāga, they will leave—</p>
              <p class="v1">the many gathered</p>
              <p class="v1">from many lands, hero,</p>
              <p class="v1">in hopes of your words.</p>
              <p>So tell them, please,</p>
              <p class="v1">how this Dhamma has</p>
              <p class="v1">been known to you.</p>
              <div class="verse-add">
                <p class="vspk">The Buddha:</p>
                <p>Subdue craving &amp; grasping—all—</p>
                <p class="v1">above, below,</p>
                <p class="v1">across, in between.<span class="fn"><a href="#stnp_note5.12.01">1</a></span><!--end fn cite--></p>
                <p>For whatever people cling to in the world,</p>
                <p class="v1">it’s through that</p>
                <p class="v1">that Māra pursues them.</p>
              </div><!--end verse-add-->
              <div class="verse-add">
                <p>So a monk, mindful,</p>
                <p class="v1">seeing these people</p>
                <p class="v1">entangled in grasping</p>
                <p class="v1">as entangled in Death’s realm,</p>
                <p>should cling to nothing</p>
                <p class="v1">in all the world,</p>
                <p class="v3">every world.</p>
              </div><!--end verse-add-->
            </div><!--end verse-->
            <p class="suttaCite">vv. 1101–1104</p><!--end suttaCite-->
            <div class="note">
              <p class="notetitle">Note</p><!--end notetitle-->
              <p id="stnp_note5.12.01">1. For Nd II’s discussion of the various meanings of the objects of craving “above, below, across, in between,” see <a href="StNp5_4.html#stnp_note5.4.03">Sn 5:4, note 3</a>. For further discussions of the many places where craving can arise, see <a href="../../DN/DN22.html">DN 22</a> and <a href="../../SN/SN35_95.html">SN 35:95</a>, note 1.</p>
            </div><!--end note-->
            <p class="seealso">See also: <a href="../../MN/MN26.html">MN 26</a>; <a href="../../MN/MN49.html">MN 49</a>; <a href="../../SN/SN4_19.html">SN 4:19</a>; <a href="../../SN/SN4_21.html">SN 4:21</a>; <a href="../../SN/SN35_115.html">SN 35:115</a>; <a href="../../SN/SN35_189.html">SN 35:189</a>; <a href="../../SN/SN35_199.html">SN 35:199</a></p>
      </div><!--end:sutta-->
